---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Checked from '../../components/Checked.astro';
import Crumbs from '../../components/Crumbs.astro';
import Newsletter from '../../components/Newsletter.astro';
import { formatDate } from '../../lib/formatDate';
import { handsOnNotes, assertHandsOnCoverage } from '../../lib/handsOnNotes';
import { hubPage } from '../../lib/hubPage';
import { withBase } from '../../lib/withBase';

const entries = await getCollection('use-cases', ({ data }) => !data.draft);
assertHandsOnCoverage(entries);
const titles = new Map(entries.map((entry) => [entry.id, entry.data.title]));
const title = 'Tested by us';
const description = 'Hands-on notes: Consensus Free, Perplexity Free, DeepL Free, LanguageTool Basic, Looka, Phrasly, Datastripes, nixm, Dessn and Spacefast.';
const notes = [...handsOnNotes].sort((a, b) => b.date.localeCompare(a.date));
const hub = hubPage(
  Astro.site!,
  Astro.url.pathname,
  title,
  description,
  notes.map((note) => ({ name: note.tool, path: `/use-cases/${note.useCaseSlug}/` })),
);
---
<Base title={title} description={description} jsonLd={hub.jsonLd} hasNewsletter>
  <article class="wrap narrow" data-pagefind-body>
    <section class="hero" style="padding-bottom:8px">
      <Crumbs items={[{ href: withBase('/'), label: 'Home' }, { label: title }]} />
      <span class="eyebrow">Hands-on notes</span>
      <h1>Tested by us</h1>
      <p class="lead">These are the only hands-on notes written on the site. Each one names the date, the tool, and what was actually tried. A shorter check does not turn the use-case page into a completed test.</p>
      <div class="meta"><Checked date={hub.dateModified} label={hub.dateLabel} /></div>
    </section>

    <section class="answer" aria-labelledby="short-answer">
      <h2 id="short-answer">Short answer</h2>
      <p>Ten notes exist. Consensus Free on 26 Oct 2026 and Perplexity Free on 2 Nov 2026 are on the research page. DeepL Free on 3 Nov 2026 is on the translate page. LanguageTool Basic on 4 Nov 2026 is on the proofread page. Looka Brand Kit on 5 Nov 2026 is on the logo page. Phrasly AI Image Detector on 6 Nov 2026 is on the image-check page. Datastripes on 7 Nov 2026 is on the spreadsheet page. nixm on 8 Nov 2026 is on the writing page. Dessn on 9 Nov 2026 is on the app-screen page. Spacefast on 10 Nov 2026 is on the vibe-code page. No other tool on this site has a hands-on note.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>The notes</h2>
      <div class="verdicts">
        {notes.map((note) => {
          const useCaseTitle = titles.get(note.useCaseSlug);
          if (!useCaseTitle) throw new Error(`Missing title for ${note.useCaseSlug}`);
          return (
            <article class="card">
              <div class="meta" style="margin-top:0">
                <span class="tag tested">Hands-on note <time datetime={note.date}>{formatDate(new Date(`${note.date}T00:00:00.000Z`))}</time></span>
              </div>
              <h3 style="font-size:1.2rem;margin-top:10px">{note.tool}</h3>
              <p>{note.tested}</p>
              <p class="caveat">{note.limits}</p>
              <p><a href={withBase(`/use-cases/${note.useCaseSlug}/`)}>{useCaseTitle}</a></p>
            </article>
          );
        })}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="prose">
      <h2>What this page is not</h2>
      <p>The research page, the translate page, the proofread page, the logo page, the image-check page, the spreadsheet page and the writing page stay marked pending. Their standard tasks have not been run. The slide-deck page, the vibe-code page and the app-screen page stay marked pending. Consensus Pro, Elicit, Gemini Notebook, DeepL Pro Individual, Grammarly Pro, Canva Pro, Google Sheets, Claude, ChatGPT, Bolt.new, Lovable, Figma, v0 and every pick that is not named above have no hands-on note. None of them has a completed standard-task note. The Looka Brand Kit note is the free logo maker, the editor, the mockup previews and the checkout prices. The paid kit was not bought, no file was downloaded, and a 1080×1080 social graphic was not made. The Phrasly note is five images on the free detector, signed out: two real photos read Likely real, two AI JPEGs were caught by a signature in the file, and the ChatGPT ramen example showed a SynthID watermark and OpenAI's signature. Pixel detection did not run on those AI files. Phrasly's over 99% accuracy figure is the vendor's claim and was not measured. A separate signature-free Midjourney-style file was not tested. The Datastripes note is one signed-out upload of a 20-row CSV. Export and saving need a sign-up. The privacy line on the page, that rows stay in the browser, was not checked by network inspection. The nixm note is one signed-out chat draft on nixm.ai. A still image needed an account and was not generated. No shareable NIXM URL appeared. Magic-link signup, the stated 20-credit grant, video, web research and signed-in stills were not tested. Vendor pages claim logged-out signals are public by link and dissolve after seven days, and some copy says a still can be made without an account. Those claims were not verified. The Dessn note is one Free-plan screen at create.dessn.ai, signed in with an email link and no card. The first frame was about 2 minutes 6 seconds after the prompt. The names, prices, steppers and £10.10 total matched the quantities on screen. Placeholder copy was added, including "Baked this morning on Mill Lane". One step showed "1 action failed" and then the screen rendered. 20 credits were still showing, and Dessn said "This first one is on us", so the credit cost was not confirmed. No export or download control was seen. Figma and v0 were not part of it. The Spacefast note is one anonymous publish, with no account, of an existing two-file HTML page. sf publish . took about 4 seconds. A one-line redeploy took about 3.2 seconds and the change was live on the first check. The plain URL returned HTTP 403, "This space is private", and the page was viewable only through a private link. The anonymous space was set to expire in about 33 hours. Making it public needs a WordPress.com account and was not tested. A plain http:// request returned HTTP 500 instead of redirecting. The pricing figures are from the vendor page. Lovable, Bolt.new and Replit were not part of it.</p>
      <p>Prices elsewhere on the site are vendor figures with a source and a checked date. They are not measurements from these notes.</p>
      <p>Browse <a href={withBase('/use-cases/')}>all use cases</a>, <a href={withBase('/best/')}>all shortlists</a> and <a href={withBase('/about/')}>how we test</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="signup"><Newsletter /></section>
  </article>
</Base>
